y first the main combat theme  is split into three parts roughly 30  seconds each the first intro part sounds  like this  [Music]  and is titled field battle easy when  striking an enemy it will react and use  these audio files labeled as easy using  these subtle notes  when it transitions to this section this  is called field battle middle  and hits on an enemy now will react with  two or three note piano trills  then it will transition into this grand  section called field battle hard  it will react with more recognizable  clacks  hoots  and symbols  now that you know let's hear in action  in an example  [Music]  now that you know you can't unhear it  this also happens when you're up against  the guardian stalker so listen carefully  the next time you're up against one did  you know that the gerudo guards are  organized by rank with the color that  they wear blue are the lowest ranked  squads green are higher ranked squads  and red denotes the squad leader and  captain of them all teak blue guards are  seen virtually everywhere but you can  see higher ranked green guards protect  more high value targets such as the  important northern ice house and  bouleara of course protecting riju this  is a pretty old secret that some players  still haven't caught but if you listen  closely to the ambient music of each  divine beast you can actually hear a  strange secret message  did you hear it it goes a little bit  something like this  [Music]  this is actually real morse code  spelling out sos or a cry for help  [Music]  funny thing is in stereo audio this  message only plays in one ear the right  side for the boys the rook and rivali  and only on the left side for the girls  mifa and urbosa this is likely a message  left by the four champions before they  die to calamity ganon which makes his  music all the more eerie every time you  listen to it additionally there's a  second message playing in the opposite  ear  fans speculate it spells sad which is  short for search an